            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A Christological title referring to Jesus Christ, symbolizing his perfect, unwavering testimony to God's truth, his role as the ultimate revealer of the Father, and his obedience even unto the point of death.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Revelation 1:5\",\"Revelation 3:14\",\"Psalm 89:37\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A designation for individual Christian believers or the Church, particularly martyrs, who bear unwavering testimony to Christ in the face of persecution.\",\"basis\":[\"Revelation 2:13\",\"Acts 1:8\",\"Revelation 11:3\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"The Holy Spirit, who bears internal and external testimony to the truth of God and the Gospel.\",\"basis\":[\"John 15:26\",\"1 John 5:6\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The term is most famously used as a direct title for Jesus Christ in the Book of Revelation. The Greek word for witness, 'martys', is the root of the English word 'martyr', connecting the concept of faithful witnessing inextricably to suffering and giving one's life for the truth.\"}",
